  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 222 PM CDT SUN AUG 2 2026\n\nUpper level trough that was providing the cloudiness across\ncentral Alabama today is forecast to cutoff into another closed\nlow, centered initially in north Georgia tomorrow. Moisture\nwrapping around the north and west side of this feature will lead\nto chances of showers and thunderstorms in the eastern part of\ncentral Alabama Monday afternoon. The upper low meanders a bit to\nour east and northeast through the middle of the week, keeping the\nbest chance of diurnal convection in the east.\n\nUltimately, the low weakens/fills and finally gets picked up by\nthe westerlies and ejects to the east by the end of the week.\nThat puts us in between two upper level high domes, one centered\nin the western Atlantic and the other centered in the Rockies. As\na result, conditions here the end of the week into next weekend\nshould be remarkably unremarkable, with temperatures and POPs very\nclose to seasonal normals.\n\n/61/",
